==Trivia ==
===In-Universe===
*In an interview with [[Tom Ruegger]] in ''Talkin' Toons With [[Rob Paulsen]]'' episode 14, he questions that Yakko might be 14 years old in a joke.
*Yakko is ambidextrous. In some episodes, he is seen writing with his left hand, and in others, he is seen writing with his right hand.
*His idol is famous actress Michelle Pfeiffer (who in the series was portrayed in the Catwoman outfit she wore in ''Batman Returns'').
*His favorite color is lavender.<ref>[[Episode 24: Yakko's World of Baldness/Opportunity Knox/Wings Take Heart#Yakko's World of Baldness|Episode 24: Yakko's World of Baldness/Opportunity Knox/Wings Take Heart]]</ref>
*Yakko is some level of lactose intolerant.<ref name="hercule yakko">[[Episode 25: Disasterpiece Theatre/Hercule Yakko/Home on De-Nile/A Midsummer Night's Dream]]</ref><ref name="the longest word"/>
*Yakko is the same height as [[Bugs Bunny]].

===General===
*Yakko's fast-talking puns are a tribute to Groucho Marx of Marx Brothers-fame.
*Yakko makes a cameo in the intro of the ''[[Pinky and the Brain]]'' spin-off series holding a magnifying glass, though only his arms are visible to create the illusion that he's an unknown scientist experimenting on the [[Pinky|two]] [[The Brain|mice]].
*Yakko appeared as an inflatable balloon display on top of the water tower in Burbank in real life, this was in promotion of the show before it was released. However, when Bob Daley, who ran the studio at the time, saw the balloon, he thought that a misshapen form of {{w|The Walt Disney Company|Disney's}} {{w|Mickey Mouse}} was sitting on top of the tower and he demanded it be removed. It was, but not before [[Paul Rugg]] took a photo. [[Water Tower#Balloon Incident|See here for more information]].
*When asked to describe his characters in one word, Rob Paulsen described Yakko as "zany."<ref>[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CsdksMNOxEw ANIMANIACS cast Q&A + SAT, JAN 16TH (2021) | 1PM PT, 4PM ET]</ref>

